            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0721" n="709" xml:id="pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.515/115: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Tuck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-20T18:00:00-04:00">June 20, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1536. For Moose. Please inform King Ibn Saud immediately that, with reference to
                    his message transmitted in Cairo’s 1667, June 17, 11 a.m., Landis is being
                    recalled to Washington to discuss the matters to which the King refers and that
                    it is hoped it will be possible promptly to take care of Saudi Arabia’s
                    immediate supply and transport requirements and to work out a satisfactory
                    long-range Saudi Arabian requirements program. Inform Landis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
